{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_14_846829933#7_1744989077","relevance":2,"reason":"Full document is dedicated to canthal tilt and gives limited direct evidence: positive canthal tilt occurs when the lateral canthus is above the medial canthus, and it can be surgically created by canthoplasty. However, it does not clearly explain why some people naturally have it beyond aging-related changes.","learned":"Positive canthal tilt is defined by the lateral canthus sitting above the medial canthus; canthoplasty can create this by repositioning/tightening the lateral canthus."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"positive canthal tilt\" (+ genetic genetics anatomical anatomy ethnicity natural))","reason":"Look for more direct explanations of natural positive canthal tilt in terms of genetics, anatomy, or ethnicity rather than surgical correction."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"positive canthal tilt\" (+ genetic genetics anatomical anatomy ethnicity natural))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_59_603346943#9_1468447829","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q2528","rank":1,"snippet":"Preventing Premature Dropping of the Canthi Types of Canthal Tilt How to Determine Your Canthal Tilt How to Prevent Premature Dropping of the Canthi Canthal Tilt Correction: Canthopexy vs. Canthoplasty Canthal Tilt Surgery and Blepharoplasty \" , \"segment\": \"Usually, the procedure involves splitting the canthal angle and cutting the lateral canthal tendon away from the lateral orbital rim. The lower lid is then shortened and a new lateral canthal angle created using stitches. During outer canthoplasty, the lateral canthus is tightened and elevated. This allows the surgeon to accurately restore a <cover>positive canthal tilt, and ideally create a more natural </cover>appearance. Lateral canthoplasty can be used during any form of lower eyelid surgery. If the patient already has a positive canthal tilt, the surgeon may still perform canthoplasty for extra support so the positive tilt will endure. As Schlessinger notes, technically standard eyelid surgery (blepharoplasty) does not address canthal tilt nor change the shape of the eye. Instead, it is meant to improve the appearance of tired or baggy eyelids. However, as Truswell points out, canthal tilt is taken into account during the initial consultation for those considering blepharoplasty. Assessing canthal tilt is an important part "}}
