{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_1370231623#2_2504750992","relevance":2,"reason":"The result is dedicated to canthal tilt and gives partial supporting evidence: positive canthal tilt is associated with youthful facial anatomy and is observed across gender and ethnicity, while neutral/negative tilt is associated with aging. It does not yet directly explain natural individual causes.","learned":"Positive canthal tilt is presented as a youthful facial feature conserved across gender and ethnicity; negative tilt is commonly associated with aging."},"action":{"op":"document","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_1370231623#2_2504750992","reason":"The page is specifically about canthal tilt and the snippet begins a 'what causes canthal tilt' section, so the full document may contain a direct answer."}}
