{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_01_131329754#8_146056079","relevance":2,"reason":"This eyelid anatomy page gives direct supporting evidence that the lateral canthal angle is normally higher than the medial canthal angle, with variation by ethnicity, which explains the anatomical basis of positive canthal tilt. However, the document is not dedicated to explaining why some people have positive canthal tilt.","learned":"Positive canthal tilt corresponds to normal anatomy in which the lateral canthal angle is higher than the medial canthal angle; the amount differs by population, e.g. about 2 mm in Europeans and 3 mm in Asians."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"canthal tilt\" (+ age aging sex gender ethnicity race) (+ normal variation morphology anatomy))","reason":"Search for sources specifically discussing natural variation in canthal tilt by age, sex, ethnicity, and anatomy, which is likely to answer why some people have positive tilt."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"canthal tilt\" (+ age aging sex gender ethnicity race) (+ normal variation morphology anatomy))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_22_854428510#0_1932998045","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q2531","rank":1,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_22_854428510#0_1932998045\" , \"end_char\": 1538.000000 , \"headings\": \"Hunter eyes Hunter eyes Contents<cover>Sex differences Attractiveness Evolution Examples References See also \" , \"segment\": \"Hunter eyes - Incel Wiki Hunter eyes From Incel Wiki Jump to navigation Jump to search Hunter eyes vs prey eyes In various lookism and blackpill forums, hunter eyes are considered to be the ideal eyes for men. They are alluring eyes, vertically narrow, deeply set, hooded, with a positive canthal tilt and an interpupil distance (IPD) within the normal </cover>range. The hoodedness of these kinds of eyes comes from a combination of a protruding brow ridge, fat tissue above the eyes, and solid 'under-eye' support caused by robust cheekbones and square orbital sockets. In technical terms, all humans have 'hunter eyes,' i.e., forward-facing eyes that allow them to focus on and pursue prey, like what is found among other predatory animals. Hunter eyes can be considered the opposite to 'prey eyes,' that is, eyes that are located on the skull's side that aids prey animals "}}
