{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_22_854428510#0_1932998045","relevance":1,"reason":"The result is about 'hunter eyes' from an incel/lookism wiki, not a reliable or dedicated explanation of positive canthal tilt. It mentions positive canthal tilt as one feature and gives adjacent facial-structure claims, but it is not strong evidence for the information need.","learned":"Some nonmedical lookism sources associate positive canthal tilt with broader orbital/facial features such as brow ridge, cheekbone support, and orbital socket shape, but trustworthiness is poor."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ \"palpebral fissure inclination\" \"palpebral fissure slant\" \"canthal tilt\") (+ ethnic ethnicity racial population sex age) (+ normal anthropometry anatomy))","reason":"Use medical/anthropometric terminology for canthal tilt to find reliable sources on normal variation by population, age, sex, and facial anatomy."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ \"palpebral fissure inclination\" \"palpebral fissure slant\" \"canthal tilt\") (+ ethnic ethnicity racial population sex age) (+ normal anthropometry anatomy))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_23_1397690825#5_3080888894","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q2532","rank":2,"snippet":"Mewing Blepharoplasty (Eyelid Lift) Canthoplasty & Canthopexy Eyebrows \" , \"segment\": \"Canthal Tilt The canthus is the pink part of your eye. The medial canthus is by your nose, and the lateral canthus is on the outside of your face. Canthal tilt is the angle between your medial and lateral canthus. If your lateral canthus is higher than your medial canthus, you have a positive canthal tilt. You have a neutral tilt when the canthi are aligned. But if your lateral canthus is lower than your medial canthus, you have negative canthal tilt. The <cover>normal male Caucasian medial canthus is about 2 mm lower than the lateral canthus (positive canthal tilt). Women have an even more positive canthal tilt, and their medial canthus is 4 mm lower than the lateral canthus. A positive canthal tilt is also known as a Mongoloid feature. Indeed, far eastern ethnic </cover>groups have a more positive tilt.\" , \"start_char\": 2097.000000 , \"title\": \"How to Get Attractive Eyes for Guys – Magnum Workshop\" , \"url\": \"https://magnumworkshop.com/how-to-get-attractive-eyes-for-guys/\" }","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_22_854428510#0_1932998045","rank":1,"relevance":1}]}}
