{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_1370231623#4_2504753484","relevance":2,"reason":"This canthal-tilt cosmetic surgery page gives direct partial evidence about why positive tilt may diminish: aging is multifactorial, and smoking/sun damage reduce eyelid tissue elasticity and supporting structures. It supports age/soft-tissue laxity as a reason some people lose positive canthal tilt, but it is not a complete explanation of why some people naturally have it.","learned":"Canthal tilt can diminish with aging and tissue laxity; smoking and sun damage may contribute by reducing elasticity in lower eyelid skin and supporting structures."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"positive canthal tilt\" (+ genetics genetic inherited hereditary facial anatomy))","reason":"Search directly for documents linking natural positive canthal tilt to inherited/genetic facial and eyelid anatomy, which would best answer why some people have it."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"positive canthal tilt\" (+ genetics genetic inherited hereditary facial anatomy))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_59_603346943#2_1468435431","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q2542","rank":1,"snippet":"to help restore a more youthful look,” Schlessinger says, “and this is achieved through canthal tilt surgery.” If you’re unsatisfied with the appearance of your eye area and considering lower or upper eyelid surgery, your surgeon will be able to assess your canthal tilt and provide you with his or her medical advice concerning the situation. Types of Canthal Tilt A person’s canthal tilt can be classified as positive, neutral, or negative, depending on the angle between the canthi. Women with attractive eyes generally have a <cover>positive canthal tilt, which means, ideally, a slight tilt at a five- to eight-degree angle between the lateral and medial canthus. “ This is youthful, feminine, and attractive,” says William H. Truswell, MD, President of the American Academy of Facial </cover>Plastic & Reconstructive Surgery ( AAFPRS ). A neutral canthal tilt occurs when no angle exists between the medial canthus and lateral canthus. “ When the line is flat it is a neutral tilt.\" , \"start_char\": 953.000000 , \"title\": \"Canthal Tilt Surgery: Preventing Premature Dropping of the Canthi\" , \"url\": \"https://www.zwivel.com/blog/canthal-tilt/\" }"}}
