{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_26_299850012#0_636416191","relevance":2,"reason":"This eyelid anatomy source gives direct anatomical support for positive canthal tilt by stating that the lateral canthal angle is normally about 2 mm higher than the medial canthal angle. However, it is a general eyelid anatomy document, not dedicated to explaining why some people have positive canthal tilt or its natural variation.","learned":"A positive canthal tilt can simply reflect normal eyelid anatomy: the lateral canthal angle commonly sits about 2 mm higher than the medial canthal angle."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"canthal tilt\" (+ \"normal values\" measurement degree degrees mm) (+ ethnicity sex women men))","reason":"Search for sources that discuss normal measured canthal tilt values and variation by sex or ethnicity, which would more directly explain why some people naturally have a positive tilt."}}
