{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_14_846829933#5_1744985815","relevance":2,"reason":"This is another segment from a canthal-tilt guide. It is related and explains neutral tilt as no angle between medial and lateral canthi, with some age/sex commentary, but it does not directly explain why some people have positive canthal tilt.","learned":"Neutral canthal tilt means the medial and lateral canthi are level; some appearance changes are discussed in terms of age and sex."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"palpebral fissure\" (+ slant inclination obliquity) (+ ethnic racial population sex age normal))","reason":"Search with medical anthropometric terminology for eye/canthus slant to find stronger evidence on normal variation by ancestry, sex, age, and anatomy."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"palpebral fissure\" (+ slant inclination obliquity) (+ ethnic racial population sex age normal))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_144139279#16_267298312","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q2554","rank":1,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_144139279#16_267298312\" , \"end_char\": 6703.000000 , \"headings\": \" \" , \"segment\": \"138005 •Concept ID: C0344482 Congenital Abnormality See: Feature record | Search on this feature Upslanted palpebral fissure MedGen UID: 98390 •Concept ID: C0423109 Finding The palpebral fissure inclination is more than two standard deviations above the mean for <cover>age (objective); or, the inclination of the palpebral fissure </cover>is greater than typical for age. See: Feature record | Search on this feature Downslanted palpebral fissures MedGen UID: 98391 •Concept ID: C0423110 Finding The palpebral fissure inclination is more than two standard deviations below the mean.\" , \"start_char\": 6129.000000 , \"title\": \"\" , \"url\": \"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/medgen/815980\" }"}}
