{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_1370231623#3_2504752287","relevance":2,"reason":"This canthal-tilt cosmetic surgery page is directly related and includes a section asking what causes canthal tilt to change over time. It says diminishing tilt is multifactorial and connects it to aging, excess eyelid skin, smoking, sun damage, and reduced eyelid/support tissue elasticity. However, it mainly explains loss of positive tilt over time, not why some people naturally have positive canthal tilt in the first place.","learned":"Diminishing canthal tilt is described as multifactorial and age-related; eyelid/support tissue laxity from aging, smoking, and sun damage can make tilt less positive or more negative."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ \"upturned eyes\" \"almond eyes\") (+ genetics inherited anatomy orbit eyelid) (+ shape natural born))","reason":"Search lay terms closely related to positive canthal tilt for pages that directly explain natural eye-shape causes, especially inherited eyelid/orbital anatomy."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ \"upturned eyes\" \"almond eyes\") (+ genetics inherited anatomy orbit eyelid) (+ shape natural born))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_50_2758809857#7_3962159947","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q2556","rank":1,"snippet":"Eyes Answer: Canthoplasty Recommended reading Everything you need to know about Eyelid Surgery Answer: Eye shape Answer: Change shape of eye to almond eye See more doctors near you \" , \"segment\": \"Almond eyes are beautifully inherited but they can also be achieved through special surgery. Consultation is necessary. https://tabanmd.com/almond-eye-surgery/ 1 person found this helpful Mehryar (Ray) Taban, MD, FACS Oculoplastic Surgeon, Board Certified in Ophthalmology ( 241) Book a virtual consultation CONTACT NOW December 10, 2017 Answer: Change shape of eye to almond eye Eye <cover>shape depends on multiple factors including eyelid and orbit anatomy. Almond eyes </cover>are beautifully inherited but they can also be achieved through special surgery. Consultation is necessary. https://tabanmd.com/almond-eye-surgery/ Helpful 1 person found this helpful Mehryar (Ray) Taban, MD, FACS Oculoplastic Surgeon, Board Certified in Ophthalmology ( 241) Book a virtual consultation CONTACT NOW Popular topics upper eyelids lower eyelids uneven ptosis droopy eye SPONSORED See more doctors near you ADVERTISEMENT\" , \"start_char\": 4337.000000 , \"title\": \"Can I Change my Eye Shape?\" , \"url\": \"https://www."}}
